alphabet: letters: 26 | vowels: 5
english alphabet: letters: 26 | vowels: 5
general: Cats say meow. Dogs bark. Red, blue, yellow, green, orange, purple, pink, black, white, brown and gray are colors. Hello, hi and hey are ways to greet someone. The head, arms, legs, hands and feet are parts of the body. Spring comes after winter and autumn comes after summer. Leaves fall from trees in autumn.
tree: A tree is a tall plant with a wooden trunk, branches and leaves.
flower: A flower is the colorful part of a plant.
star: A star is a huge ball of burning gas far away in space.
planet: A planet is a big round world that goes around a star.
road: A road is a hard path for cars, buses and bikes.
home: A home is the place where someone lives.
room: A room is a part of a building with walls, a floor and a door.
kitchen: A kitchen is the room where food is cooked.
bedroom: A bedroom is the room where people sleep.
door: A door is the part of a wall that opens so you can go in and out.
window: A window is an opening in a wall with glass that lets light in.
money: Money is what people use to buy things, like coins and paper bills.
job: A job is work that someone does to earn money.
family: A family is a group of people who are related, like parents, children, brothers and sisters.
child: A child is a young person.
children: Children is the word for more than one child.
book: A book is a set of printed pages with a story or information.
story: A story is a telling of events, true or made up.
song: A song is music with words that people sing.
music: Music is sounds put together in a pleasing way, made with voices or instruments.
movie, film: A movie or film is a story told with moving pictures.
game: A game is an activity people play for fun, often with rules.
food: Food is what people and animals eat to live.
fruit: Fruit is the sweet part of a plant that holds its seeds, like apples and oranges.
vegetable: A vegetable is a plant or part of a plant that people eat, like a carrot or a potato.
breakfast: Breakfast is the first meal of the day.
lunch: Lunch is the meal in the middle of the day.
dinner: Dinner is the meal in the evening.
months: The months are January, February, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, November and December.
today: Today is this day.
yesterday: Yesterday was the day before today.
tomorrow: Tomorrow is the day after today.
numbers: Numbers are used to count: one, two, three and so on.
half: A half is one of two equal parts.
quarter: A quarter is one of four equal parts.
nah: Nah is a casual way to say no.
thank you, thanks: Thank you or thanks is what you say when someone helps you or gives you something.
please: Please is a polite word used when asking for something.
sorry: Sorry is what you say when you feel bad about a mistake.
name: A name is the word that someone or something is called.
birthday: A birthday is the day of the year when someone was born.
language: A language is the words people use to talk and write, like English.
word: A word is a unit of language with its own meaning.
letter: A letter is a sign in the alphabet, like a, b or c. A letter is also a written message.
plan: A plan is an idea of what you are going to do and how.
goal: A goal is something you want to reach or finish.
problem: A problem is something that is wrong or hard and needs to be fixed.
mistake: A mistake is something done wrong.
test: A test is a way to check what someone knows or can do.
party: A party is a gathering where people have fun together.
gift, present: A gift or present is something you give to someone.
country: A country is a land with its own government, like Turkey, Poland or Japan.
village: A village is a small group of houses in the countryside.
world: The world is the earth and all the people and things on it.
time: Time is what we measure in seconds, minutes, hours, days and years.
pen: A pen is a tool for writing with ink.
pencil: A pencil is a tool for writing or drawing, with a gray lead inside wood.
paper: Paper is a thin material made from wood, used for writing and printing.
bag: A bag is something soft for carrying things.
box: A box is a container with flat sides, used to keep or carry things.
key: A key is a small metal tool that opens a lock.
lock: A lock is a device that keeps a door, box or bike closed until you use a key or code.
cup: A cup is a small container you drink from.
plate: A plate is a flat dish that you eat food from.
spoon: A spoon is a tool for eating soup and other soft food.
fork: A fork is a tool with points for picking up food.
soap: Soap is what you use with water to wash and clean.
shoes: Shoes are what you wear on your feet.
garden: A garden is a piece of land where people grow flowers, fruit or vegetables.
bridge: A bridge is something built over a river or road so people can cross it.
street: A street is a road in a town or city with buildings on its sides.
map: A map is a drawing that shows where places are.
picture, photo: A picture or photo is an image of something.
toy: A toy is something children play with.
doll: A doll is a toy that looks like a small person.
kite: A kite is a light toy that flies in the wind on a long string.
art: Art is things people make to be beautiful or to show ideas, like paintings and music.
sport: Sport is a physical game or activity, like football, tennis or swimming.
body: A body is all of a person or animal.
eyes: Eyes are what you see with.
ears: Ears are what you hear with.
teeth: Teeth are the hard white parts in your mouth that you bite and chew with.
medicine: Medicine is something you take to get better when you are sick.
weather: Weather is what the air outside is like: sunny, rainy, windy, hot or cold.
season: A season is one of the four parts of the year: spring, summer, autumn and winter.
dumb, stupid: Dumb or stupid is a rude way to say someone does not understand things.
